# Global ACL file - read-only archive.
#
# Format: <mailbox pattern> <identifier> <rights>
#
# Rights granted:
#   l  lookup  - folder is visible in the folder list
#   r  read    - messages can be opened and fetched
#   s  seen    - the \Seen flag can be set (so marking mail read works)
#
# Rights deliberately NOT granted:
#   w  write   - other flags cannot be changed
#   i  insert  - clients cannot append messages
#   k  create  - clients cannot create folders
#   x  delete  - clients cannot delete folders
#   t  delete  - clients cannot set \Deleted on messages
#   e  expunge - clients cannot expunge
#   a  admin   - clients cannot change ACLs
#
# Applies to IMAP clients only. mbsync writes to the Maildir directly through
# the filesystem and bypasses this entirely - which is how new mail still
# arrives in a "read-only" archive.
* owner lrs
